WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.400
- What about free will?

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.410
- Free will is also a nice exercise.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.340
Free will is an illusion that we,

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.403
A.I. people are gonna solve.

00:00:13.923 --> 00:00:15.430
- (Interviewer) So, what do you think,

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.880
once we solve it, that
solution will look like?

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.381
Once we've put it in the page?

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:20.214
- (Guest) It's going to look like...

00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:22.746
First of all, it will look like a machine.

00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:25.190
A machine that acts as though

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.050
it has free will.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.700
It communicates with
other machines as though

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.650
they have free will,

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.000
and you wouldn't be able
to tell the difference

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.704
between a machine that does
and a machine that doesn't

00:00:36.704 --> 00:00:37.833
have free will.

00:00:39.485 --> 00:00:40.318
- (Interviewer) So, the
illusion, it propagates

00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:42.470
the illusion of free will amongst

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.551
the other machines?

00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:46.263
- (Guest) And faking it is having it.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.053
Okay?

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:49.650
That's what true
intelligence is all about.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.363
Faking intelligence is intelligence,

00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:55.590
because it's not easy to fake.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.420
It's very hard to fake, and you can only

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.159
fake if you have it.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.409
- (laughs)

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.960
That's such a beautiful statement.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.043
(laughs)

00:01:10.368 --> 00:01:12.896
You can't fake it, if you don't have it.

00:01:12.896 --> 00:01:13.729
(laughs)

